From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_LOG_FLUSH_MS set: the guest thread watchdog copies each process's thread list under its list lock and logs it after letting go (same lines); unset as before

T175d. 0009's watchdog logs every guest thread every 15 s (40 times) while it holds the process's
thread list lock. With every log line written to /data at once (the front's log_flush_line), a
line waits whenever the disk does (after the before-play pass about a second a write), and each of
those waits held the lock guest threads take to start, end or list threads. With the front's
EDEN_UP_LOG_FLUSH_MS set (any value but empty or starting with 0) the list is copied under the lock
(thread id, core, state, wait reason, pc, lr, sp) and logged after it is let go: the same lines in
the same order. Unset: as before. core.cpp is not a translation id input and no name is added to
TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/core/core.cpp b/src/core/core.cpp
index 2c82d3279a44635aeb03cfda049393b4c38f0107..9af1119f9207b47a3be1414ebcc49fc076612693 100644
--- a/src/core/core.cpp
